That is frequently underestimated.

Detection Opportunities
Sign-in telemetry

Alert on:

first-seen source IP
first-seen country
unusual ASN
impossible travel
unusual user agent
browser fingerprint changes
login during abnormal working hours
legacy authentication
unusual device state
successful login following repeated failures
Data-access telemetry

Once authenticated, look for:

recursive directory access
unusually high file counts
mass downloads
access across unrelated business units
ZIP/archive generation
broad search queries
rapid folder enumeration
sustained download sessions
download volume exceeding historical baseline
Identity telemetry

Look for:

password-only authentication to sensitive systems
stale accounts
non-expiring passwords
users without MFA enrollment
accounts exempt from Conditional Access
unmanaged devices
sign-ins from devices never seen before
Example Detection Logic
IF application IN [ShareFile, ownCloud, Nextcloud]
AND authentication_method = password_only
AND source_ip = first_seen
AND files_downloaded > baseline * 3
THEN
    severity = CRITICAL
    revoke_session
    disable_account_temporarily
    alert_SOC
    begin_infostealer_investigation
Better Detection Model

A more mature model would calculate:

Risk =
Identity anomaly
×
Authentication weakness
×
Data sensitivity
×
Download deviation
×
Device trust

For example:

New country                  +25
Unmanaged device             +20
No MFA                       +30
First-seen IP                +15
100x download baseline       +40
Defense documents accessed   +50

The exact weighting is something I would keep proprietary to InfinityGrid.

