Endpoint-to-Identity Correlation

This is one of the biggest lessons.

If EDR detects:

Lumma
RedLine
Vidar

the SOC should automatically ask:

Which credentials were accessible from this machine?

Then:

EDR detection
     ↓
Identify logged-in users
     ↓
Enumerate browser-stored credentials
     ↓
Enumerate active SaaS sessions
     ↓
Revoke tokens
     ↓
Reset credentials
     ↓
Review post-infection cloud logins

That workflow should be automated wherever possible.

Attack Breakers
Phishing-resistant MFA

Strongest straightforward breaker.

Prefer:

FIDO2 security keys
passkeys
certificate-backed authentication

over:

SMS OTP
email OTP

for high-value repositories.

Conditional Access

Require:

managed devices
compliant device posture
approved countries
trusted network conditions where appropriate
Session Risk Detection

If account behavior changes sharply after authentication, don't assume MFA solved the problem.

Password Rotation After Infostealer Detection

Any credential accessible from an infected endpoint should be treated as potentially compromised.

Token Revocation

Rotating a password without revoking active sessions can leave the attacker authenticated.

Least Privilege

A normal employee should not be able to download an entire corporate document repository.

Download Thresholds

Mass export should trigger:

step-up authentication
SOC notification
temporary throttling
administrative approval where justified
