Defender Questions
Can any corporate file-sharing account still authenticate with only a password?
Are there MFA exceptions?
Are stale users disabled?
Are vendor/service accounts covered by MFA?
Does EDR trigger credential-reset workflows after infostealer detection?
Are browser sessions revoked?
Can employees download thousands of files without alerting anyone?
Do you know whether employee credentials are present in stealer logs?
Can administrators identify every SaaS session associated with a compromised endpoint?
How quickly can identity access be killed across every cloud application?
InfinityGrid Takeaway

The Zestix campaign demonstrates a problem vulnerability scanners cannot solve:

There may be nothing to patch.

The platform can be current.

The server can be hardened.

The vulnerability scan can be clean.

And the attacker can still sign in through the front door using credentials the organization never invalidated.

For modern enterprise environments:

Credential validity is part of vulnerability management.
